Plan for Developing a Multi-Agent AI System for FizioMidia. We will build this using existing MERN architecture without rewriting FizioMidia. I recommend developing a multi-agent system in which three specialized AI agents operate independently but communicate through your existing Express backend.

Agent 1 — Physiotherapy AI Assistant
Purpose: Provide educational physiotherapy guidance to members and guests in English and Kiswahili.
Capabilities:
- Answer questions about musculoskeletal conditions, neurological rehabilitation, cardiorespiratory physiotherapy and other physiotherapy subjects.
- Explain common symptoms without diagnosing the user.
- Provide general exercise education and safe movement advice.
- Explain when physiotherapy assessment is appropriate.
- Explain when someone should seek emergency medical attention.
- Educate users about stroke rehabilitation, back pain, posture, sports injuries and other topics.
- Explain how to find registered physiotherapists on FizioMidia.
- Support English and Kiswahili conversations.
Important safety restrictions:
- No definitive diagnosis.
- No medication prescriptions.
- No individualized treatment prescriptions or unsupported exercise plans.
- No claims that massage or any other intervention cures a condition.
- Escalate emergency warning signs, such as sudden facial drooping, arm weakness or speech difficulties, to immediate emergency medical care.
- Make clear that AI advice does not replace assessment by a qualified healthcare professional.
I recommend connecting this agent to a verified physiotherapy knowledge base rather than allowing it to rely entirely on its general AI training.

Agent 2 — Forum Content Creator
Purpose: Maintain regular, high-quality educational discussions across FizioMidia forum subcategories.
Scheduled automation

Proposed workflow:
1. Read all available forum subcategories.
2. Check previously published topics to avoid repetition.
3. Select an appropriate topic for each subcategory.
4. Research and prepare an educational discussion.
5. Check factual accuracy and potential medical misinformation.
6. Save the generated topic as a pending publication.
7. Send an email to the administrator containing the topic and approval link.
8. Wait for human approval.
9. Publish the topic through the existing forum API.
10. Record publication status and administrator activity.

For example:
Forum subcategory	Example daily topic
Musculoskeletal	Understanding lower back pain
Neurological	Rehabilitation after stroke
Sports Physiotherapy	Preventing ankle injuries
Pediatric Physiotherapy	Motor development in children
Cardiorespiratory	Breathing exercises and their role
General Health	Physical activity and healthy ageing

You should be able to configure the schedule for each subcategories to receive daily content, but Never allow this agent to publish medical education direct, Agent should send Email or WhatsApp message to Admin then Admin review it for any change and edit before publishing

Agent 3 — Virtual Administrator
Purpose: Monitor FizioMidia activity and assist the human administrator.
Human supervised


This is potentially the most valuable agent operationally.

It could monitor:
Application area	AI responsibility
User registrations	Identify unusual registration patterns
Physiotherapists	Monitor pending verification applications
Appointments	Identify booking anomalies
Forum	Detect spam, harassment and suspicious content
Messaging	Identify unusual messaging activity using authorized metadata
Sponsored products	Identify suspicious submissions
Promotions	Monitor expiry and status
System health	Monitor API errors and unusual activity
Administration	Prepare daily activity summaries

For example, every morning it could email you:
- New member registrations.
- New physiotherapist applications awaiting approval.
- New clinics registered.
- New forum posts and reported content.
- Appointment activity.
- Promotions expiring soon.
- Suspicious activities requiring attention.
- Backend errors and unusual traffic.
Important: It should initially operate in read-only mode. It can recommend actions, but cannot approve physiotherapists, delete accounts, suspend users, or modify financial or administrative records without explicit human authorization.

