Agent communication
The agents should not necessarily communicate with each other for every task.

Instead, use a central orchestrator that assigns work to the appropriate agent.

For example:
- A member asks about back pain → Physiotherapy Agent.
- A scheduled job requests educational content → Forum Agent.
- A monitoring job requests a daily report → Virtual Admin Agent.
- Forum Agent submits a topic for publication → Approval Service.
- Human admin approves → Existing Forum Controller publishes it.


Database collections
I recommend introducing these collections:
Collection	Purpose
AIConversations	Conversation sessions
AIMessages	Chat history
AIGeneratedContents	Drafts and publication status
AIActivityLogs	AI actions and decisions
AIConfigurations	Agent settings, schedules and limits
AIKnowledgeDocuments	Verified educational knowledge

You can also reuse your existing user, forum, notification and admin-log models wherever appropriate.


Human approval system for the Forum Agent
This is particularly important because FizioMidia publishes healthcare education.

I would implement the following approval workflow:
1. Content generation
   
   Agent prepares a topic for a specific forum subcategory.
2. Automated quality checks
   
   Check language, duplication, factual consistency, safety and references.
3. Save draft
   
   Store it with status pending_review.
4. Email administrator
   
   Send the complete draft with a secure review link.
5. Human verification
   
   Admin can approve, edit, reject or request regeneration.
6. Forum publication
   
   Approved content is published using the existing forum controller.
7. Audit record
   
   Save the administrator's decision, timestamp and publication ID.


The administrator dashboard should also include:
- Pending AI content.
- Approved content.
- Rejected content.
- Regeneration requests.
- Publication history.
- Agent activity.

Virtual Admin: monitoring without compromising control
The Virtual Admin should have a dedicated dashboard inside your existing admin panel.

I would divide its permissions into three levels:
Permission	Initial access
Read application statistics	Allowed
Generate recommendations and reports	Allowed
Flag suspicious activity	Allowed
Draft administrative notifications	Allowed
Suspend or delete users	Human approval
Approve physiotherapists	Human only
Modify appointments or financial records	Human only

One important design principle: use conventional code for monitoring and detection wherever possible. For example, appointment counts, expired promotions, failed requests and pending approvals should be calculated using MongoDB queries, not guessed by an AI model.

The AI should interpret those results and prepare useful recommendations.


